        <tr class="d-block">
    <td
      class="d-block color-fg-default comment-body markdown-body js-comment-body"
      
    >
        <h2 dir="auto">Motivation:</h2>
<ol dir="auto">
<li>Incremental verification for a relatively large and existed codebase.</li>
<li>Minimize changes to executable codes</li>
<li>Improve readability of executable codes for non-verification developers. Do not mix the use of executable code and ghost code.</li>
<li>Avoid extra efforts to install verus toolchain (verus, verusfmt, customized rust-analyzer) for non-verification developer.</li>
<li>Allow project to avoid adding verus (builtin, builtin-macro, and vstd) as a hard dependencies. Projects can easily define their verus_stub procedure macros to control the verus dependency by feature.</li>
</ol>
<h2 dir="auto">Summary</h2>
<p dir="auto">All attribute-base procedure macros only change or insert codes to enable verification when compiling with erase.keep() == true and will not have side effect (verus_spec) or return empty token stream (proof!{}, proof_xxx!{}) when erase.keep() == false</p>
<p dir="auto"></p><div class="Box Box--condensed my-2">
  <div class="Box-header f6">
    <p class="mb-0 text-bold">
      <a href="https://github.com/verus-lang/verus/blob/c3014c7b5df1e3d70eab4339f4b8fd26360e0499/source/builtin_macros/src/lib.rs#L260-L313">verus/source/builtin_macros/src/lib.rs</a>
    </p>
