<br>
Two attribute procedure macros:<p></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>#[verus_spec(...)]: Add specification signature.</li>
<li>#[verus_verify(...)]: Add hints to verifier to mark verifier(external), verifier(external_body), verifier(rlimit(xx)), etc. In additionally, dual_mode is specified via verus_verify.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Three function-like procedure macros:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>proof!{...}: proof block similar to proof { ... } inside verus macro</li>
<li>proof_decl!{...}: proof block with function-scoped variables</li>
<li>proof_with!{...}: pass and receive tracked/ghost</li>
</ul>
<h2 dir="auto">Syntax and examples</h2>
<h3 dir="auto">Basic specification signature on function item</h3>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">verus_spec</code> will mark the function #[verifier::verify] and insert specifications for the function (e.g., ensure, requires, etc.).</p>
