<p></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>
<p dir="auto">When a function is anotated with verus_spec(with ...), verus_spec procedure macro will generate two version of functions: verus_verified_{xxx} and {xxx} to allow the function to be used by functions inside and outside verification scope.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir="auto">The unverified function requires false so that not providing correct proof_with!() to pass the tracked/ghost variables to the function will fail the verification.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="#[verus_spec]
fn call_unverified(x: u32) {
  test_mut_tracked(0); // FAILS
}"><pre class="notranslate"><span class="pl-c1">#<span class="pl-kos">[</span>verus_spec<span class="pl-kos">]</span></span>
